# OWD SEO standards (mandatory)

Full rules: `docs/build-standards.md` and `docs/post-build-seo-check.md`. Read `AGENTS.md`.

## Gate
- `npm run build` runs `astro build && node scripts/seo-gate.mjs`.
- Non-production (local, preview, staging, PR Action) prints every issue as a warning and exits 0.
- `VERCEL_ENV=production` fails only for the criticals in the README SOP (render, noindex vs `SITE_INDEXABLE`, wrong canonical/sitemap domain, broken links and key-page 404s, placeholder output, dead forms, secrets, missing favicon, missing branded 404). GTM/GA4/pixel, titles, descriptions, OG, alt, and schema are warnings.
- `SITE_INDEXABLE=true` only in Vercel Production on launch day. Never set it, or `VERCEL_ENV`, in GitHub. The PR Action must not fail on warnings.
- If you touch `scripts/`, run `npm run test:gate`.

## Must
- All business facts come from `src/config/site.ts` only. Never hand-type NAP or phone numbers into pages.
- No invented business facts: no made-up reviews, ratings, aggregateRating, license numbers, street address, awards, years, or areas.
- Client-facing previews contain no internal notes, TODOs, draft labels, lorem ipsum, or "replace this" text.
- Every page: one title (30-60 chars; homepage = service + area + brand), description 140-160 (no em dashes), one absolute self-referencing canonical on the production host with a trailing slash, OG + Twitter tags, `<html lang>` from config, exactly one h1.
- JSON-LD from config: LocalBusiness subtype + WebSite sitewide, BreadcrumbList inner pages, Service on service pages, FAQPage only where the FAQ is visible.
- Noindex three ways on previews (meta, dynamic robots.txt, X-Robots-Tag for *.vercel.app). No static public/robots.txt.
- Images in repo via astro:assets; no hotlinks; alt on content images; width/height; hero eager + fetchpriority high.
- Trailing slash always; internal links in final form; zero broken links; nothing but the site in dist/ (no .md, .pdf, drafts, inspiration/ in public/).
- GTM only when indexable, ID from PUBLIC_GTM_ID. Preview-only widgets only on previews.
- Content visible without JS (.reveal pattern), landmarks, skip link, 44px tap targets.

## Nav
- Services AND Service Area are both dropdowns on desktop and nested the same way in the mobile menu.
- Every top-level nav item, dropdown triggers included, uses the one shared class `.nav-link`. Never style nav with structural selectors.
- Only one dropdown open at a time; triggers are buttons with aria-expanded.
- Mobile hamburger has a visible "MENU" label. Header phone on desktop; tap-to-call button on mobile.
